.TH AETHERSDR "1" "2026-06-20" "AetherSDR" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
AetherSDR \- FlexRadio transceiver client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aethersdr
.br
.B aethersdr --config
.I command
.RI [ key ] " " [ value ]
.br
.B aethersdr --aetherd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AetherSDR brings FlexRadio operation to Linux without Wine or virtual machines.
Built from the ground up with Qt6 and C++20, it speaks the SmartSDR protocol
natively and aims to replicate the full SmartSDR experience.
.SH CONFIG COMMANDS
Settings live in a SQLite store under the user config directory
(\fB~/.config/AetherSDR/AetherSDR.db\fR). The \fB--config\fR mode
inspects or repairs them without starting the GUI and then exits:
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIprefix\fR]
Print every setting as key<TAB>value, optionally filtered by key prefix.
.TP
.B get \fIkey\fR
Print one value (exit status 2 if the key does not exist).
.TP
.B set \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Create or change a setting, verifying it persisted.
.TP
.B unset \fIkey\fR
Delete a setting.
.TP
.B export
Sanitized dump of the whole store (secrets redacted); diagnostic output,
not a restorable backup.
.TP
.B path
Print the settings database path.
.SH HEADLESS ENGINE
\fB--aetherd\fR starts \fBaetherd\fR, AetherSDR's headless engine, in place of
the application, with the remaining options passed to it (\fB--aetherd --help\fR
lists them). The engine serves radio control to local clients over a
current-user socket and shows no window. It ships in the ARM64 AppImage, beside
the application; where it is absent, \fB--aetherd\fR exits with status 127.
.PP
Run from the AppImage under systemd, set \fBKillMode=mixed\fR and
\fBPrivateTmp=yes\fR in the unit. The AppImage's mount process sits in the same
control group and unmounts the image when it receives \fBSIGTERM\fR; \fBmixed\fR
sends \fBSIGTERM\fR to the engine alone, so it can release the radio before the
image goes away. \fBmixed\fR then kills the mount process, which can leave its
mount behind; \fBPrivateTmp\fR keeps that mount inside the unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage: https://github.com/aethersdr/AetherSDR
